      <h2>I Oppose Proposition 50</h2>
      <p><strong>Written on:</strong> October 31, 2025</p>

      <p>I oppose Proposition 50.</p>

      <p>Response to gerrymandering in Texas should not be tit-for-tat.</p>

      <p>A simple solution would be to implement proportional representative elections for the number of seats allocated to each state.</p>

      <p>In the case of California’s 52 seats, this would mean a party getting 25% of the votes would get 13 seats. Interestingly, 51 of those seats would require 1.92% of the votes, while the 52nd seat would only need a max of 0.96%.</p>

